  description: Roentgenium is a chemical element with symbol Rg and atomic number
    111. It is an extremely radioactive synthetic element (an element that can be
    created in a laboratory but is not found in nature); the most stable known isotope,
    roentgenium-282, has a half-life of 2.1 minutes. Roentgenium was first created
    in 1994 by the GSI Helmholtz Centre for Heavy Ion Research near Darmstadt, Germany.
